{
  "id": "30324_tobinoru",
  "headword": "{飛|と}び{乗|の}る",
  "reading": "とびのる",
  "romaji": "tobinoru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to jump onto; to hop on; to leap aboard",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to jump onto; to hop aboard (a train, bus, horse)",
      "explanation": "To get onto something in one quick leap, typically a vehicle that is about to leave or already moving. The nuance is haste, not athletic skill."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "30324_tobinoru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{電車|でんしゃ}に{飛|と}び{乗|の}った。",
      "english": "I jumped onto the train.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30324_tobinoru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{発車|はっしゃ}まぎわのバスに{飛|と}び{乗|の}る。",
      "english": "To hop onto a bus just as it is pulling out.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30324_tobinoru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{知|し}らせを{受|う}けて、{近|ちか}くに{止|と}まっていたタクシーに{飛|と}び{乗|の}って{病院|びょういん}へ{向|む}かった。",
      "english": "On getting the news, I jumped into a taxi parked nearby and headed for the hospital.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A compound of {飛|と}ぶ (to jump, to fly) and {乗|の}る (to board, to ride). The thing boarded is marked with に.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive. Takes に for the vehicle, not を: {電車|でんしゃ}に{飛|と}び{乗|の}る, never ✗{電車|でんしゃ}を{飛|と}び{乗|の}る.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {電車|でんしゃ}に{飛|と}び{乗|の}る: to jump onto a train\n- {自転車|じてんしゃ}に{飛|と}び{乗|の}る: to hop on a bicycle\n- {馬|うま}に{飛|と}び{乗|の}る: to leap onto a horse\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {飛|と}び{降|お}りる: to jump off — the paired opposite\n- {駆|か}け{込|こ}む: to rush in — running into a train or building, without the leap",
